course: dictionary
lesson: 14371
title: Orally: by speech or by mouth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Orally is an adverb that tells you how something is done. It means by speaking, out loud, not in writing. «Mia answered the question orally, so she said her answer to the class instead of writing it down.» The clue is said and not written, so orally means by speech.
explain: Orally has a second meaning, used in medicine. «The doctor said, take this medicine orally.» Look at the clues: medicine and take. Swap in by mouth and the sentence still makes sense, so orally means by mouth, not by injection.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Orally comes from oral, which is about the mouth or speech, so the two meanings are linked.
fact: Orally means by speech, not in writing, or by mouth, as with medicine.
fact: «Present your project orally» means tell it out loud to your class.
fact: Stories passed down orally were told out loud, from person to person, before people wrote them down. This is called oral tradition.
fact: «Take this medicine orally» means swallow it by mouth, not as an injection.
fact: To check the meaning, swap in by speech or by mouth. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
exercise: «The teacher asked us to answer the questions orally.» What does orally mean here? | By singing a song | *By speaking out loud | By writing on paper | By drawing a picture
exercise: «The nurse said the tablet must be taken orally.» What does orally mean here? | In writing on the label | *By mouth | By injection into the arm | Under the bed
exercise: «The old story was passed down orally for hundreds of years.» Which word means by speech, not in writing? | story | years | old | *orally
test: Ben read his poem orally to the class. What does orally tell you about how Ben shared it? | Ben sent it by email | Ben drew it in a picture | Ben wrote it on the board | *Ben spoke it out loud
test: «The village stories were passed on orally, long before they were written down.» Which meaning fits orally best? | *By being spoken from person to person | By drawing pictures on walls | By reading a book silently | By text message
exam: «Maya's grandad told her the family tale orally, so she learned it by listening, not by reading.» What does orally mean in this sentence? | By computer | In a song | In writing, on paper | *By speech, out loud
